---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — ArNega"
  description="Draft terms of use for the ArNega desktop application and website."
  path="terms"
>
  <Nav home={false} />
  <main class="container prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Draft — v0.1</p>

    <p class="notice">
      This is a developer-provided starter document, not professional legal advice. It will be
      refined as the project matures.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By downloading or using the ArNega application or this website, you agree to these terms. If
      you don’t agree, don’t use them.
    </p>

    <h2>The software</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>ArNega is provided free of charge for personal use on your own devices.</li>
      <li>
        The source code’s license status is stated in the repository; “free to download” does not
        by itself grant redistribution or commercial-use rights beyond what the repository license
        (once chosen) specifies.
      </li>
      <li>
        ArNega depends on third-party software you install separately — notably Ollama and the AI
        models it downloads — each governed by its own license terms.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      ArNega is provided <strong>“as is”, without warranty of any kind</strong> — express or
      implied — including fitness for a particular purpose. AI-generated answers can be wrong;
      you are responsible for verifying anything you rely on.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the ArNega developers shall not be liable for any
      damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, the software or website — including
      decisions made based on AI answers, data loss, or consequences of violating rules that apply
      to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to use ArNega in compliance with applicable laws and the rules that bind you (see
      <a class="link-accent" href="responsible-use">responsible use</a>), and not to use it to
      infringe others’ rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated alongside new releases; the version published with the current
      release applies.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer home={false} />
</Base>
